237 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (The primary components of the Electronic Throttle System include the Accelerator Pedal Position Sensor \(APPS\) and the Electronic Throttle Body itself, which contains the butterfly valve responsible for regulating the airflow into the engine. We use an APPS from Williams Controls, which is attached to the accelerator pedal housing. It consists of two inductive rotary position sensors along with a signal conditioning circuit that outputs the positions of both independent sensors. These signals are sent to the MoTeC M800 ECU, which then calculates the target position of the butterfly valve in the ETB.)
/E (The primary components of the Electronic Throttle System include the Accelerator Pedal Position Sensor \(APPS\) and the Electronic Throttle Body itself, which contains the butterfly valve responsible for regulating the airflow into the engine. We use an APPS from Williams Controls, which is attached to the accelerator pedal housing. It consists of two inductive rotary position sensors along with a signal conditioning circuit that outputs the positions of both independent sensors. These signals are sent to the MoTeC M800 ECU, which then calculates the target position of the butterfly valve in the ETB.)
/Pg 17 0 R
>>
endobj
238 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
